{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789909640,"nonce":"pRPDJUheqTSk1wWm0+v4ANneN4U=","title":"TestRest: `haxe.Rest.get_length` calls an unrenumbered `fn82` after the stdlib merge","message":"In the conformance harness module set, TestRest fails at run time with\n`uncompiled \u003clambda_unit__1\u003e`. `RAYZOR_DUMP_MIR=1` shows\n`haxe.Rest.get_length` in module 41 calling `fn82`, which is the\n`array_length` MIR-wrapper forward reference; when the stdlib module is\nmerged into the program the reference is neither renumbered nor bound by\nname, so it stays a stub. The same program compiles alone\n(haxe-conformance/regressions/RestArgs.hx passes), so the drop depends on\nthe merge order in the large module set.\n\nRepro: `haxe-conformance/run.sh --only TestRest` on a `--llvm --release`\nbuild; `RAYZOR_DUMP_FN_PTRS=1` names the stub.","files":null}]}